{
  "summary": "Finished the Build-stage round-1 work for the Identity switch: the earlier backend work was verified green and the front-end was migrated from JWT/refresh-token auth to ASP.NET Core Identity cookie sessions. ApiService is now cookie-only (credentials:'include', no Authorization header, no refresh-on-401; a 401 clears the AuthStore and surfaces a plain 'Sign in required.' message). AuthApi talks to the new endpoints (login, register, me, logout, providers, forgot-password, reset-password, change-password) and surfaces RFC 7807 field errors. AuthStore keeps the session in memory (no tokens in localStorage). AuthGuard resolves the session from the server via authApi.me() before rendering, routes Public/disable paths (login, signup, forgot-password, reset-password), forces /change-password while mustChangePassword is set, and renders children with no check in desktop mode. login/signup/forgot-password/reset-password pages were rewritten; a new change-password page and a new Admin-only Team page (list page=20, add teammate with temporary password, role change with optimistic-concurrency expectedRole, activate/deactivate with confirmation, paged ResponsiveTable) were added; AppShell drops setAccessToken, signs out via authApi.logout() before clearing, and shows a role-aware (Admin-only) Team menu item. Team.module.css and the shared auth CSS classes were added. Front-end: tsc clean, next lint clean, next build succeeds with the /team and /change-password static routes, all 248 jest tests pass. Backend: full dotnet test re-run is green (903 passed, 75 skipped, MariaDB-gated). No kickbacks.",
